<?xml version="1.0"?>
<ScenContainer xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema">
  <ScenTitle>The Battle of Seogeom-ri, 2015</ScenTitle>
  <ScenDescription>&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;&lt;P&gt;This scenario presents a fictional clash between South Korean and North Korean forces.&amp;nbsp; At stake is the South Korean island of Seogeom-ri, which lies close to the border between the two countries.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"&gt;-------------------------------------------------------&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Because the weapons control order at the beginning of the scenario is WEAPONS HOLD (FIRE ONLY IN SELF-DEFENSE), the scenario begins with South Korea's attack options set at "No AI Attacks."&amp;nbsp; You are free to fire against any units that are attacking you, but you must either control the attacks&amp;nbsp;manually or remove the "No AI Attacks" restriction in the Orders menu.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;The&amp;nbsp;amphibious landing can only be accomplished if the &lt;EM&gt;Hyang Ro Bong&lt;/EM&gt; is moved as close as possible to the southern shore of&amp;nbsp;Seogeom-ri.&amp;nbsp; This may require the player to engage in some careful piloting when she gets close to the island.&amp;nbsp; You will know you have accomplished the landing because your ground units will appear on the island.&amp;nbsp; Other things may happen, too.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&amp;nbsp;A delta template .ini file has been included in the .zip file to assist in updating the scenario to any future versions of the database.&amp;nbsp; &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"&gt;Scenario Author: Mark Gellis&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;</ScenDescription>
